# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Xbox port: ROM-derived files the inherited list above does not reach.
#
# This project is distributed as SOURCE ONLY -- users supply their own
# baserom.us.z64 and build everything. Every pattern below was added because
# tools/audit_repo_clean.py PROVED the file's bytes are present in the ROM,
# not because it looked suspicious. Run that script before publishing.
#
# All of it comes back with:  python tools/extract_rom_bins.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw texture payloads. `/textures/**/*.png` and `*.bin` were already ignored,
# but the extractor also drops uncompressed N64-format payloads whose
# extension names the format, and those were being published. The filename is
# the ROM offset (7F1124.i4 lives at 0x7F1124), which is what makes them
# trivially recoverable.
/textures/**/*.i4
/textures/**/*.i8
/textures/**/*.ia1
/textures/**/*.ia4
/textures/**/*.ia8
/textures/**/*.ia16
/textures/**/*.ci4
/textures/**/*.ci8
/textures/**/*.rgba16
/textures/**/*.rgba32

# The same texture data again, as C hex. `/textures/**/*.bin` was already
# ignored, and 278 of these 279 files decode to EXACTLY the .bin sitting next
# to them -- the ignore list covered the data in one form and published it in
# the other. The Makefile generates these into $(BUILD_DIR) from the .png
# (n64graphics, Makefile:591), so the copies in the source tree are stale
# build output and nothing needs them.
/textures/**/*.inc.c

# Blender exports of course geometry: ROM display lists converted to models.
# One track is 34 MB of .blend (334 MB unpacked), and it is regenerated by the
# Makefile's model_extract target, so it has no business in the repo.
/models/**/*.zip
/models/**/*.blend

# Generated Xbox build inputs. The wrappers themselves hold no ROM data (they
# are .incbin lines and #includes), but the payloads they point at do.
/Platform/xbox/gen_seg/*.bin
/Platform/xbox/gen_seg/*.mio0

# gen_asmwrappers bakes ABSOLUTE incbin paths (the integrated assembler
# resolves them against the compiler's working directory, which RXDK controls,
# so relative ones do not work). That makes these files machine-specific: they
# point at the author's own checkout and resolve nowhere on anyone else's.
# Worse, a missing .incbin is dropped SILENTLY while its label is still
# emitted, so the symbol aliases the next asset instead of failing the build.
# Always regenerate; never publish. setup.py runs this every time.
/Platform/xbox/gen_asm/*.c

# gen_segblobs writes the same kind of wrapper for the four MIO0 segments, and
# bakes the same absolute paths. Published, they carry one machine's directory
# and every other build rewrites them, so a clean clone is dirty the moment it
# is built. setup.py regenerates them every run.
/Platform/xbox/gen_seg/*_blob.c

# Build and verification logs
*.log

# bin/audiobanks.us.bin (ROM 0x966260) and bin/audiotables.bin (ROM 0x979AA0)
# are verbatim ROM segments. `/bin/*` above already covers them; the
# `!bin/*.bin` negation that used to re-admit them has been removed.

# torch is fetched by setup.py, never committed
tools/torch/
